Package: subsampleIRT
Type: Package
Title: Target-Specific Optimal Subsampling for Penalized Item Response Models
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: person("Zili", "Liu", email = "ZLiu20@mdanderson.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Penalized marginal maximum likelihood for multidimensional,
    multi-group mixed two- and three-parameter logistic item response models
    with Gauss-Hermite quadrature, and target-specific optimal subsampling for
    large-scale assessment data. A pilot fit and one pass of person-level
    scores give sampling probabilities that minimize the subsampling variance
    of a chosen target (item difficulties, discriminations, guessing
    parameters, latent correlations, group means or a joint target). The
    package fits the inverse-probability weighted criterion with a fixed
    Horvitz-Thompson normalizer, computes conditional sandwich standard
    errors, chooses the subsample size by a two-stage precision rule and fits
    penalty paths on one subsample.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: Matrix, stats
NeedsCompilation: no
